  ('jubilee', '/ˈdʒuːbɪli/', '[''celebration'', ''jubilate'']', '[''unjubilee'', ''disjubilee'']', 'a special anniversary of an event, especially one celebrating twenty-five or fifty years of a reign or activity', 'lễ kỷ niệm', 'The city celebrated its silver jubilee with a grand parade.', '{IELTS}', 'C1', 'Abstract'),
