  ('juxtapose', '/ˌdʒʌkstəˈpəʊz/', '[''compare'', ''juxtaposition'']', '[''unjuxtapose'', ''disjuxtapose'']', 'to place different things side by side for contrasting effect', 'đặt cạnh nhau, so sánh', 'The exhibition juxtaposes Picasso''s early drawings with his later works.', '{IELTS}', 'C2', 'Verbs'),
