  ('displace', '/dɪsˈpleɪs/', '[''replace'', ''preempt'', ''fire'', ''give notice'', ''can'']', '[''hire'', ''begin'', ''place'']', 'to force to move from the usual or proper place; to take the place of', 'thay thế, di dời', 'Thousands of people were displaced by the war.', '{IELTS}', 'C1', 'Verbs'),
