  ('embrace', '/ɪmˈbreɪs/', '[''accept'', ''embracing'', ''embracement'', ''bosom'', ''encompass'']', '[''reject'', ''uncover'', ''nonembrace'', ''unembrace'']', 'to accept or support a belief, theory, or change willingly; to hug', 'chấp nhận, ôm', 'The company embraced new technology quickly.', '{IELTS}', 'B2', 'Verbs'),
