  ('get', '/ɡɛt/', '[''obtain'', ''acquire'', ''receive'', ''gain'', ''fetch'']', '[''terminate'', ''give'', ''lose'', ''forfeit'', ''release'']', 'Offspring.', 'lấy', 'The word get appeared several times in the article.', '{IELTS}', 'A1', 'Nouns'),
  ('would', '/wʊd/', 'could', NULL, 'Past tense of ''will''; used in conditionals or polite requests.', 'sẽ (quá khứ), có lẽ', 'I would appreciate your help.', '{IELTS}', 'A1', 'Grammar'),
  ('she', '/ʃiː/', '[''woman'']', '[''unshe'', ''disshe'']', 'A female.', 'cô ấy', 'Pat is definitely a she.', '{IELTS}', 'A1', 'Nouns'),
  ('how', '/haʊ/', 'in what way', NULL, 'In what manner or way; to what degree or extent.', 'thế nào, như thế nào', 'How do you get to school every day?', '{IELTS}', 'A1', 'Grammar'),
  ('some', '/sʌm/', 'several', 'none', 'An unspecified quantity or number; a certain amount.', 'một vài, một ít', 'Some people prefer tea over coffee.', '{IELTS}', 'A1', 'Grammar'),
  ('them', '/ðʌm/', '[''both'']', '[''unthem'', ''disthem'']', '(plural) Those ones.', 'họ', 'The word them appeared several times in the article.', '{IELTS}', 'A1', 'Pronouns'),
