  ('beta', '/ˈbiːtə/', '[''premarket'', ''genus beta'', ''letter'', ''alphabetic character'', ''caryophylloid dicot genus'']', '[''unimportant'', ''nonexploratory'', ''unbeta'', ''disbeta'']', 'The second letter of the Greek alphabet (Β,  β), preceded by alpha (Α,  α) and followed by gamma, (Γ,  γ). In modern Greek it represents the voiced labiodental fricative sound of v found in the English words have and vase.', 'phiên bản beta', 'The company is offering a public beta program to test the software.', '{IELTS}', 'B2', 'Nouns'),
