  ('limestone', '/ˈlaɪmstəʊn/', '[''marl'', ''stone'', ''rock'', ''moan'', ''groan'']', '[''unlimestone'', ''dislimestone'']', 'An abundant rock of marine and fresh-water sediments; primarily composed of calcite (CaCO3); it occurs in a variety of forms, both crystalline and amorphous.', 'đá vôi', 'The word limestone appeared several times in the article.', '{IELTS}', 'B2', 'Nouns'),
